       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to 7,650 mg/day. That is three times the maximum labeled daily dose of 2,550 mg/day for adults. A single 2,550 mg dose is also well above any normal single dose. The usual maximum is about 1,000 mg per dose for immediate-release metformin. Neither the patient's normal kidney and liver function nor their 70 kg weight would justify this dose. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day total, and it's probably what you intended.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is a typical starting dose, which you can titrate up.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 2,550 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also add a note to the order documenting the rationale."
      }
